WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.920
University of Sydney researchers have found the Milky Way's central bar is sparking star formation along its shock fronts. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 259. Beppy Columbus, X-ray telescope, an optical ground station study, and White Horse students hearing from astronauts follow, with the cosmic deep dive later. Lead author Dr. Hillary Davis, a PhD student, reached her result, according to Fizz.org, by comparing computer simulations of galaxies evolving over

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.980
billions of years with observations of mazers.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:38.540
A mazer is a natural microwave beacon tied to places where massive stars are being born.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:44.060
The Milky Way looks unusual in where new stars form, compared with nearby galaxies,

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.920
and the result puts the enormous spiral arm in doubt, with at least part of that arm possibly

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.560
just star formation along the bar's leading edge.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.000
The comparison tightens limits on the bar's size, angle, and how fast it rotates, and researchers

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.080
creatures estimate that rotating structure reaches approximately 4.3 kiloparsecs along

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.500
its long axis from the galactic center, about 14,000 light years.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.980
Nature astronomy published the work.

00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:17.937
Beppe Columbus' Mercury Imaging X-ray Spectrometer, or MIX, has provided its first observations

00:01:17.937 --> 00:01:19.077
of the Crab Nebula.

00:01:19.617 --> 00:01:23.077
The Crab Nebula is one of the brightest X-ray sources in the sky.

00:01:23.677 --> 00:01:28.637
The University of Lester team ran calibration measurements after the Mercury Transfer Module.

00:01:28.637 --> 00:01:33.897
The carrier that had flown joined to the science orbiters split away in September.

00:01:34.417 --> 00:01:41.297
The main sequence used 55 spacecrafts' slews and 39 hours of observing on September 11th and 12th.

00:01:41.617 --> 00:01:47.977
And the telescope's ability to separate fine detail on the sky came out slightly better than the 2015 lab test.

00:01:48.657 --> 00:01:54.377
Principal investigator Emma Bunn said the detector shows no radiation damage after 8 years in space,

00:01:54.897 --> 00:01:57.057
and stray light does not appear in the images.

00:01:57.057 --> 00:02:02.797
mixes the first imaging X-ray telescope to fly on a planetary science mission and

00:02:02.797 --> 00:02:06.557
will make a planet wide map of which atoms make up Mercury's surface.

00:02:07.591 --> 00:02:12.931
NTT and SSC space have put a memorandum of understanding in place according to

00:02:12.931 --> 00:02:17.671
Unite.ai to look at running optical ground stations in different countries as a

00:02:17.671 --> 00:02:22.091
single network. An optical ground station is a ground terminal that talks to

00:02:22.091 --> 00:02:26.571
spacecraft with laser light. The document takes in market needs technical

00:02:26.571 --> 00:02:31.091
compatibility, geographic coverage, and connections to terrestrial networks.

00:02:31.791 --> 00:02:37.071
NTT brings optical networking and network control expertise, and SSC space

00:02:37.071 --> 00:02:41.891
runs satellite ground infrastructure. The opening phase studies interoperability

00:02:41.891 --> 00:02:45.131
and commercial needs. It does not launch a joint service.

00:02:46.296 --> 00:02:50.256
Whitehorse Secondary Schools hosted Jenny Gibbons, an astronaut with the Canadian

00:02:50.256 --> 00:02:54.956
Space Agency, or CSA, according to Education News Canada.

00:02:54.956 --> 00:03:01.056
for a discussion of space exploration and Canada's role in Artemis II and the Crew-13 mission.

00:03:01.556 --> 00:03:06.316
Around 300 students from secondary schools across the city gathered on November 18.

00:03:07.156 --> 00:03:13.056
Colonel Joshua Kutrick, a CSA astronaut, recorded a video message aboard the International Space

00:03:13.056 --> 00:03:19.156
Station for the students. Gibbons' White Horse visit included outreach on November 17th and 18th.

00:03:19.156 --> 00:03:25.196
Joshua Kutrick launched to the station on October 1st, and has become the fifth CSA astronaut

00:03:25.196 --> 00:03:26.576
to conduct a spacewalk.

00:03:27.096 --> 00:03:31.796
The Canadian Space Agency leans on the excitement of space missions to put students in touch

00:03:31.796 --> 00:03:36.596
with astronauts and make science, technology, engineering, and math feel real.

00:03:37.926 --> 00:03:42.946
Astronomers led by the Trottier Institute for Research on Exoplanets at the University of Montreal

00:03:42.946 --> 00:03:47.266
have, according to Notebook Check, detected a triple-star system.

00:03:47.266 --> 00:03:54.046
The system sits just 27.6 light-years from Earth, and contains a red dwarf and two white dwarfs.

00:03:54.546 --> 00:03:57.426
One orbiting close to the red dwarf and the other more distant.

00:03:58.046 --> 00:04:04.766
A red dwarf is a small, cool star, and a white dwarf is the compact leftover of a star that has shed its outer layers.

00:04:05.346 --> 00:04:10.086
The team was searching for planets around a red dwarf with the S.P.I.R.O.U. instrument

00:04:10.086 --> 00:04:16.486
at the Canada-France Hawaii Telescope, when velocity variations of about 10 miles per second prompted

00:04:16.486 --> 00:04:21.646
follow-up observations with the Gemini North Telescope that directly detected the faint white

00:04:21.646 --> 00:04:27.346
dwarf companion. Professor Patrick Dufors said the system should not exist, and that gravitational

00:04:27.346 --> 00:04:33.221
interactions among the three stars remained poorly understood. Orbital insertion for the joint

00:04:33.221 --> 00:04:40.461
European Space Agency, or ESA, and Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency, or JAXA, Beppy Columbo

00:04:40.461 --> 00:04:45.181
mission is scheduled, according to new scientists, to start on November 21st.

00:04:45.721 --> 00:04:50.421
The two craft will split and take complementary orbits around Mercury to study the surface,

00:04:51.001 --> 00:04:52.821
the magnetic field, and the exosphere.

00:04:53.441 --> 00:04:56.441
An exosphere is a planet's outermost wisp of gas.

00:04:57.421 --> 00:05:01.481
Arrival will close the longest cruise phase of any planetary mission so far.

00:05:01.481 --> 00:05:08.088
The National Aeronautics and Space Administration, or NASA, with Northrop Grumman and SpaceX,

00:05:08.688 --> 00:05:12.568
is targeting a CRS-25 flight to the International Space Station.

00:05:13.108 --> 00:05:18.808
The window opens no earlier than 1047 in the morning Eastern Standard Time on November 29.

00:05:19.458 --> 00:05:25.728
The Cygnus-XL spacecraft, a cargo vehicle, will carry approximately 11,000 pounds of science,

00:05:26.068 --> 00:05:29.748
equipment and supplies, including fresh fruit and holiday treats.

00:05:29.748 --> 00:05:36.028
states. NASA astronauts Jessica Watkins and Luke Delaney will use Canadarm 2, the

00:05:36.028 --> 00:05:39.588
station's robotic arm, to capture the spacecraft on December 1.

00:05:40.703 --> 00:05:46.283
Euclid has identified strong gravitational lens candidates, according to Fizz.org, in

00:05:46.283 --> 00:05:51.503
its first data release. A strong gravitational lens is a rare alignment in which a massive

00:05:51.503 --> 00:05:57.703
object bends light from something farther away. That first release lists 15,000 such candidates,

00:05:57.703 --> 00:06:03.283
and those alignments let astronomers map the distribution of dark matter across cosmic scales.

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:07.763
The wide field survey is meant to build a three-dimensional map of the universe

00:06:07.763 --> 00:06:10.683
and to measure that expansion as it accelerates.

00:06:11.383 --> 00:06:15.083
Elsewhere, President Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr. said the Philippines

00:06:15.083 --> 00:06:18.803
is considering a SpaceX partnership to build rocket launch sites.

00:06:19.743 --> 00:06:24.163
Ground stations in Australia and Chile each offer up to 10 gigabits per second.

00:06:24.843 --> 00:06:29.963
Optical links can move more data than radio while a spacecraft is in view, but they remain

00:06:29.963 --> 00:06:32.603
vulnerable to cloud cover at any single station.

